  "natspec": {
    "functions": {
      "0xd11f519c": {
        "notice": "Registers a new strategy with a target allocation. Admin-only.",
        "dev": "Reverts with {StrategyManagerStrategyNotEmpty} if the strategy already reports a balance, and bubbles the revert if its `totalAssetsManaged()` read fails.",
        "params": {
          "strategy": "Address of the strategy to register.",
          "targetBps": "Target allocation in basis points (0–10 000)."
        }
      },
      "0x2d600e21": {
        "notice": "Clears the deposit latch, reopening the vault's deposits unless the vault's own manager-swap latch (`IVaultCoreRecovery`) is also set. Admin-only (DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE, the role that gates `removeStrategy`).",
        "dev": "Clear it once the force-removed strategy's funds are back in the vault or written off: deposits then price on a NAV that no longer moves when those funds return. Reverts with {StrategyManagerDepositLatchNotSet} if the latch is not set."
      },
      "0xfe32d662": {
        "notice": "Returns true while a force removal keeps the vault's deposits closed.",
        "dev": "Consumed by VaultCore, which closes deposit/mint and reports `maxDeposit`/`maxMint` as 0 while set."
      },
      "0xb49a60bb": {
        "notice": "Returns the list of all registered strategy addresses."
      },
      "0x89355a28": {
        "notice": "Returns the target allocation in basis points for a given strategy.",
        "params": {
          "strategy": "Strategy address to query."
        }
      },
      "0x4641257d": {
        "notice": "Snapshots the current allocated balance across all strategies and emits Harvested.",
        "dev": "Anyone can call; does not move funds. Useful for off-chain indexers."
      },
      "0x7d7c2a1c": {
        "notice": "Rebalances the vault's asset distribution to match strategy target allocations.",
        "dev": "Pushes or recalls assets to/from strategies, then calls `deploy()` on each strategy that advertises `IProtocolAdapter` and holds idle asset. Anyone can call. A recall that loses value beyond a fixed rounding tolerance reverts with {StrategyManagerWithdrawShortfall}; an honest partial recall emits {StrategyPartiallyRecalled}; a failing deploy emits {StrategyDeployFailed}. Allocations are capped at the vault's actual idle balance."
      },
      "0xd2c725e0": {
        "notice": "Returns true while a `rebalance()` is in progress (the reentrancy guard is held).",
        "dev": "Consumed by VaultCore to reject share-price-sensitive operations (deposit/mint/ withdraw/redeem) mid-rebalance, defeating read-only reentrancy via a strategy callback. Deliberately NOT part of IStrategyManager, so the interface's ERC-165 id is unchanged."
      },
      "0x175188e8": {
        "notice": "Removes a registered strategy. Admin-only.",
        "dev": "Reverts with {StrategyManagerStrategyStillAllocated} while the strategy reports a balance. A strategy whose `totalAssetsManaged()` read fails is force-removed instead, emitting {StrategyForceRemoved}; any funds it still holds leave the vault's NAV. The force removal latches the vault's deposits closed (`IStrategyManagerRecovery`): exits reopen, capped at idle, while deposit/mint stay closed until the admin calls `clearDepositLatch`, so no new depositor shares in funds the strategy returns in the meantime. Those funds accrue to whoever still holds shares when they return; a holder who exits while latched is priced on the idle-only NAV and gives up their share of the stranded funds. The strategy cannot be re-added while it reports a balance.",
        "params": {
          "strategy": "Address of the strategy to remove."
        }
      },
      "0x6817031b": {
        "notice": "Sets the vault address. Admin-only (DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE).",
        "params": {
          "_vault": "Address of the ERC-4626 vault this manager serves."
        }
      },
      "0x45f7f249": {
        "notice": "Returns the sum of `IStrategy.totalAssetsManaged()` across all registered strategies.",
        "dev": "Trust assumption: strategies are trusted to report accurate balances. Reverts if any strategy's read reverts or the sum overflows, which makes a VaultCore vault's `totalAssets()` revert (fail closed)."
      },
      "0x5e02d602": {
        "notice": "Returns the current sum of all registered strategy target allocations in basis points."
      },
      "0x8420bd02": {
        "notice": "Updates the target allocation for a registered strategy. Admin-only.",
        "params": {
          "newBps": "New target allocation in basis points.",
          "strategy": "Address of the registered strategy."
        }
      },
      "0xfbfa77cf": {
        "notice": "Returns the address of the associated vault."
      }
    },
    "notice": "Diamond facet managing yield strategy allocations for a single ERC-4626 vault.",
    "dev": "All logic lives in StrategyManagerLib. This contract is a pure delegator. Initialization order in the consumer's Diamond initializer: 1. AccessControlLib.__AccessControl_init(admin) 2. StrategyManagerLib.__StrategyManager_init() 3. (Optional) StrategyManagerLib._setVault(vault) The StrategyManager must be configured as the vault's strategy manager via `IVaultCore.setStrategyManager(address(this))` before calling `rebalance()`. `allocateToStrategy` is guarded by `_checkManager()` which checks the caller address, not any role — granting DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE is neither necessary nor sufficient. Each Lattice protocol adapter must name this diamond as its operator (`setOperator`): `rebalance()` recalls through the adapter's `withdraw` and deploys its idle through `deploy`, both operator-gated. A force removal latches the vault's deposits closed until the admin calls `clearDepositLatch` ({IStrategyManagerRecovery}, a separate interface so IStrategyManager's ERC-165 id is unchanged)."
  },
